*   **Vendor Renegotiation:** With 20 months of runway, you have leverage. Approach your largest vendors (cloud hosting, marketing agencies, etc.) and negotiate better rates in exchange for longer-term commitments.
*   **Marketing ROI Optimization:** Review your customer acquisition cost (CAC) across all channels. Pause or cut spend on low-performing marketing channels and double down only on the highest-converting ones.
*   **Strategic Hiring & Contractor Use:** Implement a temporary freeze on non-essential hiring. For necessary roles, consider using fractional executives or contractors instead of full-time hires to save on benefits and overhead.
*   **Cloud/Infrastructure Optimization:** If you are a tech company, cloud hosting costs can spiral. Have your engineering team audit AWS/GCP/Azure usage to eliminate idle instances and optimize storage.

**Next Steps for your Presentation:**
I recommend presenting the 20-month runway as a "baseline" scenario, and then showing a "target" scenario where implementing 2-3 of the cost reduction options above drops the burn rate to ~$40K/month, effectively extending your runway to 30 months. 

