### 2. Runway Extension & Cost Reduction Options
To back up the narrative, you can present the following strategic options to the team or board:

**Option A: Revenue-Driven Runway Extension (Top-Line Focus)**
Since your revenue is already strong ($670K/quarter or ~$223K/month), small improvements in revenue will have a massive impact on your $62K/month burn rate.
*   **Upselling/Cross-selling:** Focus on expanding contracts with existing customers, which has a lower Customer Acquisition Cost (CAC) than acquiring new ones.
*   **Pricing Optimization:** Consider a slight price increase for new tiers or legacy customers, which drops directly to the bottom line.
*   **Accelerated Receivables:** Offer small discounts for upfront annual payments instead of monthly billing to immediately boost cash reserves.

**Option B: Operational Cost Reductions (Bottom-Line Focus)**
*   **Vendor & SaaS Audit:** Review all software subscriptions, cloud hosting (AWS/Azure), and third-party tools. Consolidate redundant tools and negotiate better rates for annual commitments.
